    "explanation": "To both parties: this case cannot be safely decided on the evidence, so it goes to a human reviewer. Here is why, in plain terms.\n\nThe only measurement of how far the vehicle actually travelled comes from the driver's GPS trace (EV-GPS-00110). That artifact is impaired. It contains a single 428-second dropout from 18:35:00 to 18:42:08, the fixes on either side of it are 6.9 km apart in a straight line, and the gap covers the whole KPE tunnel segment in dispute. A gap over 90 seconds engages POL-RD-07(a), so the trace is impaired for POLICY purposes, not merely by the admissibility pre-pass; both things are true and I say both. It carries weight 0.39 and the issue codes GPS_GAP and LOW_COVERAGE, and the discount is applied throughout.\n\nMeasured the way POL-RD-07(i) directs - a straight line across the gap, the reading most favourable to the driver - the trip is 21.2 km against an optimal 18.4 km, an excess of 2.8 km or 15.2%, under POL-RD-01's 20% gate. The driver is right that on that reading no deviation is established. But that figure is a floor, not a measurement. The admissibility record for the same trace states that a surface route between the two bounding portals would put the trip at 25.5 km, which is over the gate. Nothing in the bundle distinguishes the two readings. So the excess can neither be established nor excluded: the limb is undecided, and under POL-RD-07(iii) that is a data failure, not a finding for the driver.\n\nPOL-RD-07(ii) permits a deviation on an impaired trace only with an independent source, and there is none. The chat (EV-CHAT-00110, weight 0.6, TRUNCATED_LOG) stops at 18:26:14, before the tunnel, and holds no admission - only the driver's 'going KPE ah boss' and the rider's 'ok'. The gantry itemisation on the fare (EV-FARE-00110, weight 0.75, PARTIAL_RECORD) is null, so the charged-gantry check cannot run. The 21.2 km on the trip record and the 21.2 km on the fare are copies of the impaired trace, which POL-RD-07(ii) excludes as circular. The driver's statement ('I took the KPE like always') denies a detour rather than conceding one, so it is not the route admission the clause names. The traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00110-01, weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) is absent. POL-RD-10(3) therefore makes escalation mandatory, and POL-RD-10(1) requires it independently, because the fact the case turns on rests on a 0.39-weight artifact, below the 0.70 floor.\n\nOn the driver's remaining points: the $3.00 ERP is not refunded separately, because erp_gantries is null, the gantry match is undecidable on the record, the line is treated as matched, and no billing-integrity finding arises. No repeat-deviation pattern is established (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d 0 against completed_trips_90d 744), so there is no POL-RD-06(b) uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral. No pickup or dropoff amendment exists, so POL-RD-05 is unavailable. The driver's claim that he simply followed the platform's 'KPE then ECP' optimal corridor, and the rider's own '18-19 km' estimate, are both attempts to answer the one question the tunnel gap leaves open, and neither can answer it. The rider's enhanced-corroboration trigger under POL-RD-08 (deviation_claims_60d 1, substantiated 0) is not engaged.\n\nEscalation is terminal: no refund and no driver payment issues, and the disputed $34.42 is held, not collected or refunded, pending human review. What would settle it: the fare's gantry itemisation showing which gantries were crossed, an untruncated chat covering the tunnel, or a trace that records the tunnel segment itself. No referral is issued, because no clause produces one on these facts."
  },
