    "explanation": "Addressed to both parties. This dispute cannot be decided on the present record and goes to a human reviewer. The $34.42 stays held: it is neither collected from the rider nor refunded to him, and no money moves now. The blocker is the driver's GPS trace (EV-GPS-00110). It carries a single 428-second gap between consecutive fixes (18:35:00-18:42:08), far over the 90-second limb of POL-RD-07, and that gap sits over the whole KPE tunnel stretch you dispute. The artifact is impaired at the schema layer too: weight 0.39, issue codes GPS_GAP and LOW_COVERAGE (coverage_pct 81.7). Both are named here, as POL-GEN-02(3) requires. Read the POL-RD-07(i) way - a straight line between the bounding fixes, the reading most favourable to the driver - the trip is 21.2 km against an 18.4 km optimal: 2.8 km, or 15.2%, under POL-RD-01's 20% gate. On that reading the driver is right and no deviation is established. But that reading is a floor, not a measurement of what was driven inside the tunnel: a surface route between the same two portals would make the trip 25.5 km, over the gate, and nothing in the bundle tells us which was driven. Because the trace is impaired, POL-RD-07(ii) forbids establishing a deviation on it alone. No independent corroboration exists. The chat (EV-CHAT-00110, weight 0.6, TRUNCATED_LOG) stops at 18:26:14, 2186 s before the trip ended, and contains no admission - only the driver's 'going KPE ah boss' and the rider's 'ok'. erp_gantries on the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-00110, weight 0.75, PARTIAL_RECORD) is null, so the gantry-route check cannot be run. trip_record.actual_distance_km is a copy of the trace figure, which POL-RD-07(ii) excludes as circular. The driver's own statement admits taking the KPE - the optimal corridor - so it confirms his account of the route rather than measuring the tunnel stretch; it answers a limb that names a counterparty statement, but it cannot stand in for the distance. Two triggers therefore fire. POL-RD-07(iii) with POL-RD-10(3): an impaired trace with no corroborating source of the kind POL-RD-07(ii) names makes the absence of proof a data failure, not a finding for the driver. And POL-RD-10(1) with POL-GEN-02(2): any ruling on the excess rests on EV-GPS-00110 at 0.39, which caps confidence below the 0.70 floor. On the remaining points: the $3.00 ERP stands - erp_gantries being null, POL-RD-09(4) treats the line as matched, and the trip record's optimal-route ERP is also $3.00, so there is no phantom gantry, no billing-integrity refund and no referral on that ground. POL-RD-05 is unavailable (the amendment fields are all null). POL-RD-06 raises no repeat-deviation pattern (deviation_flags_90d 0 over 744 completed trips), so there is no FULL_REFUND uplift and no driver-conduct referral. The enhanced-corroboration rule in POL-RD-08 is not engaged (deviation_claims_60d 1). The driver is right that a NO_ACTION would leave the charge in place, but escalation replaces the ruling, so the charge is held rather than kept. What would settle it: the missing KPE/ECP traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00110-01, weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT), a complete chat export covering the tunnel window, or an itemised erp_gantries list showing whether the vehicle crossed the on-corridor gantries or a surface alternative."
